{
    "background_story": "Elisabeth was a gentle soul with a green thumb and a love for all things botanical. She spent most of her days tending to her lush garden, where hollyhocks towered above the other flowers, their stately spikes a favorite of hers. As a child, Elisabeth would help her grandmother, a skilled herbalist, harvest the hollyhock flowers to make soothing teas and salves. The hollyhock's majestic beauty and versatility inspired Elisabeth to become a botanist, studying the plant's unique properties and uses. She went on to develop a line of natural remedies, featuring the hollyhock as a key ingredient. Elisabeth's passion for the hollyhock and her dedication to sharing its benefits with others earned her the nickname 'The Hollyhock Lady' among her community.",
